      "result": "<task id=\"ses_f4a154b75ffe3rYm55eoUzOmtI\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# BlockNote Editor Capability Inventory — A2E Suite\n\nScope note: the document editor for `a2e-documents` is the **shared BlockNote `BLOCK_SCHEMA`**, instantiated inside `RichTextFieldEditor`. Evidence: `document.object.ts:47-48` defines the `content` field as `FieldType.RICH_TEXT`; `FieldWidgetRichTextEditor.tsx:88-92` passes the field name to `RichTextFieldEditor`; `RichTextFieldEditor.tsx:198` passes `schema: BLOCK_SCHEMA` to `useCreateBlockNote`. The a2e-documents app itself has no BlockNote dependency; it reuses twenty-front's editor (app `package.json` has no `blocknote` entry).\n\nInstalled version: `@blocknote/*` `0.51.4` (`packages/twenty-front/package.json:33-36`; `node_modules/@blocknote/core/package.json:14`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. BlockNote schema actually used\n\n**Definition** — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/blocks/Schema.ts:11-21`:\n- `...defaultBlockSpecs` spread at `Schema.ts:13`\n- custom `callout: CalloutBlock()` at `Schema.ts:14`\n- custom `file: FileBlock()` at `Schema.ts:15` (overrides the default `file`)\n- `...defaultInlineContentSpecs` at `Schema.ts:18`, plus custom `mention: MentionInlineContent` at `Schema.ts:19`\n- style specs are not overridden, so `defaultStyleSpecs` applies (BlockNote defaults; see `node_modules/@blocknote/core/types/src/blocks/BlockNoteSchema.d.ts:17`).\n\n**Enabled default block specs** — full list at `node_modules/@blocknote/core/types/src/blocks/defaultBlocks.d.ts:2-191`:\n- `audio` (:3), `bulletListItem` (:20), `checkListItem` (:32), `codeBlock` (:48), `divider` (:53), `file` (:54), `heading` (:68, levels 1-6 per :74), `image` (:88), `numberedListItem` (:113), `paragraph` (:129), `quote` (:141), `table` (:149), `toggleListItem` (:154), `video` (:166).\n\nSo available formats: H1-H6 headings (+ toggle headings), paragraph, bullet/numbered/check lists, toggle list, quote, code block, divider, table, image, video, audio, file, and custom callout. Nested/indented blocks are structurally supported (child blocks are walked recursively at `exportFidelity.ts:86` and `getBlockLevelDiff.ts:10`).\n\n**Enabled inline content** — `defaultBlocks.d.ts:318-327`: `text` and `link`; plus custom `mention`.\n\n**Enabled styles** — `defaultBlocks.d.ts:196-315`: `bold`, `italic`, `underline`, `strike`, `code`, `textColor`, `backgroundColor`.\n\n**Custom specs**:\n- Callout: `CalloutBlock.tsx:30-39` (`type: 'callout'`, `content: 'inline'`, `emoji` prop, emoji cycle at :28).\n- File: `FileBlock.tsx:41-56` (`type: 'file'`, `content: 'none'`, props `url`/`name`/`fileCategory`).\n- Mention: `MentionInlineContent.tsx:84-105` (`type: 'mention'`, props `recordId`/`objectMetadataId`/`objectNameSingular`/`label`/`imageUrl`).\n\n**Surfaced in the slash menu** — `getSlashMenu.ts:32-56` maps icons for H1-H6, Toggle Headings, Callout, Toggle List, Divider, Quote, Numbered/Bullet/Check List, Code Block, Paragraph, Table, Image, Video, Audio, Emoji; `File` is replaced with the custom file insert at `getSlashMenu.ts:66-86`.\n\nDistinct editor (do not confuse): the standalone/dashboard rich text uses a restricted schema `DASHBOARD_BLOCK_SCHEMA` at `page-layout/widgets/standalone-rich-text/constants/DashboardBlockSchema.ts:3-13` (paragraph, heading, bullet/numbered/check list, code, table, quote only).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Multi-column authoring (BlockNote 0.51)\n\n**Not offered by default.** `defaultBlockSpecs` contains no `column`/`columns` spec — enumerate `defaultBlocks.d.ts:2-191` (none present).\n\n**The capability exists only in `@blocknote/xl-multi-column@0.51.4`**, which is installed but only transitively:\n- Package present: `node_modules/@blocknote/xl-multi-column/` (package version `0.51.4`).\n- It exports `multiColumnSchema` and `withMultiColumn`, adding `column` and `columnList` block specs: `node_modules/@blocknote/xl-multi-column/src/blocks/schema.ts:9-32`.\n- Spec definitions: `node_modules/@blocknote/xl-multi-column/src/blocks/Columns/index.ts:7-28` (`ColumnBlock`, `ColumnListBlock`); slash items `.../extensions/SuggestionMenu/getMultiColumnSlashMenuItems.tsx:30`.\n- Installed because the exporters depend on it: `yarn.lock:4742` (`xl-docx-exporter` → `@blocknote/xl-multi-column`) and `yarn.lock:4779` (`xl-pdf-exporter` → `@blocknote/xl-multi-column`); resolution at `yarn.lock:4753`.\n\n**Not enabled in the app.** `@blocknote/xl-multi-column` is absent from `packages/twenty-front/package.json` (verified; block is `:33-36`), `BLOCK_SCHEMA` never calls `withMultiColumn` (`Schema.ts:11-21`), and no first-party source imports the package — the only repo references are the unintegrated `Inspiration apps (bureaubilan)/Texxel-main/...` files. **Multi-column authoring: absent.**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Math / diagrams (KaTeX / LaTeX / mermaid)\n\n- **`@blocknote/xl-math`: absent.** Not under `node_modules/@blocknote/` (only `core, mantine, react, server-util, xl-docx-exporter, xl-multi-column, xl-pdf-exporter`); no `xl-math` entry in `yarn.lock`; no math block in `defaultBlockSpecs`.\n- **KaTeX: present in `node_modules` but only from documentation tooling, not the editor.** `yarn why katex` → `micromark-extension-math@3.1.0` and `rehype-katex@7.0.1`; `yarn why remark-math` → `@mintlify/cli` / `@mintlify/common` / `@mintlify/mdx`; `yarn why rehype-katex` → `@mintlify/mdx`. None is a twenty-front or BlockNote dependency. **No editor math rendering.**\n- **mermaid: absent.** `node_modules/mermaid` does not exist and there is no `mermaid` entry in `yarn.lock` or any first-party `package.json`. The only traces are the Shiki *syntax-highlighting grammar* `node_modules/@shikijs/langs/package.json:209` and a `rollup` devDependency mention of `@mermaid-js/mermaid-cli` (`node_modules/rollup/package.json:159,162`) — neither renders diagrams.\n- **MathJax: absent** from the workspace (`node_modules/mathjax` missing); only referenced by the unintegrated `Inspiration apps (bureaubilan)/Texxel-main/apps/web/package.json:68`.\n- No math/katex/latex/mermaid references anywhere in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor` or `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Export controls\n\nAll under `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/export/`. The menu exposes **three** formats (`BlockEditorExportMenu.tsx:108-173`):\n\n| Format | How produced | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **PDF (print)** | Browser `window.print()` on the live editor DOM; adds body class `a2e-print-editor` | `BlockEditorExportMenu.tsx:137-147` (class `:142`, `window.print()` `:144`, label `Export as PDF (print)` `:162`) |\n| **DOCX** | `@blocknote/xl-docx-exporter` `DOCXExporter` + `docxDefaultSchemaMappings` | `exportBlocksToDocxBlob.ts:1-34` (importer `:1-4`, exporter `:18-24`, `toBlob` `:31`) |\n| **Markdown** | BlockNote's own lossy converter `editor.blocksToMarkdownLossy` | `exportBlocksToMarkdown.ts:9-15` |\n\nMIME types: `text/markdown;charset=utf-8` and the DOCX OOXML type (`BlockEditorExportMenu.tsx:64-66`). Download helper: `exportBlocksToMarkdown.ts:17-45`. **ODT: absent** — no `@blocknote/xl-odt-exporter` in `yarn.lock` (only the unintegrated Texxel inspiration app declares it).\n\n**Separate library PDF path** (not in the editor menu): `command-menu-item/record/single-record/utils/exportBlockNoteEditorToPdf.ts:1-50` uses `@blocknote/xl-pdf-exporter` `PDFExporter` (`:17`) + `@react-pdf/renderer` `pdf()` (`:48`) + `file-saver` `saveAs` (`:49`), invoked by `ExportNoteSingleRecordCommand.tsx:36-39`. It builds a bare `BlockNoteEditor.create({ initialContent })` **without `BLOCK_SCHEMA`** (`:13-15`), so custom specs are unmapped.\n\n**Fidelity warning mapping** — `exportFidelity.ts`:\n- Warning keys: `'callout-degrades' | 'file-omitted' | 'mention-degrades'` (`:11-14`).\n- Format matrix (`:35-42`): `pdf: []`, `docx: ['callout-degrades','file-omitted','mention-degrades']`, `markdown: ['callout-degrades','file-omitted','mention-degrades']`.\n- Detection: `callout` → `callout-degrades` (`:121-123`); `file` → `file-omitted` (`:125-127`); inline `mention` → `mention-degrades` (`:129-140`).\n- Localized labels (`BlockEditorExportMenu.tsx:95-99`):\n  - `'callout-degrades'`: `Callouts degrade to plain paragraphs`\n  - `'file-omitted'`: `File blocks are omitted`\n  - `'mention-degrades'`: `Mentions degrade to plain text`\n- `ALWAYS_EXPORTED_BLOCK_TYPES = ['image','table','file','video','audio']` (`:24-30`); menu is hidden for an empty document (`:87`, `:153-155`).\n\n**Known degradation prose**: `exportBlocksToMarkdown.ts:6-8` — “callouts/toggles degrade to plain paragraphs”; `exportBlocksToDocxBlob.ts:14-17` — default mappings are widened for custom specs. Toggles are not in the warning set but are flagged as degrading in the Markdown comment.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Font / page-layout / print controls\n\n- **User-facing font-family/size controls for the BlockNote document editor: absent.** Only static styling exists: `.editor { font-size: 13px }` (`BlockEditor.tsx:59-64`), menu `font-family: theme.font.family` (`:129-138`), inline `code { font-family: monospace; font-size: 0.9rem }` (`:163-171`), callout emoji `font-size: 18px` (`CalloutBlock.tsx:15-21`). a2e-documents front components only use theme font tokens for their own widget chrome (`document-page.front-component.tsx:53-63,221`; `document-browser.front-component.tsx:71,634`).\n- **Page size, margins, headers, footers: absent.** No such terms/controls found in the editor or app source.\n- **Print stylesheet:** the export path adds the class `a2e-print-editor` to `<body>` (`BlockEditorExportMenu.tsx:142`), but **no CSS rule defines `a2e-print-editor` anywhere in first-party source** (the only occurrence is that line) — the print-specific styling hook is effectively a no-op. There is no editor-level `@media print`. Existing `@media print` rules only hide app chrome: `PageLayoutRecordIdentifierBar.tsx:70`, `PageLayoutTabsRenderer.tsx:39,54,83,119`, `PageLayoutGridLayout.tsx:91` (plus `page-break-inside: avoid` at `:107`), `MainAppLayoutWithSidePanel.tsx:20,40`, `PageCardLayout.tsx:21,42,81,97,116`, `DefaultLayout.tsx:31,46,57,68`, `RecordTableWithWrappers.tsx:25`, `MobileNavigationBar.tsx:34`, `SidePanelTabStrip.tsx:35`, `StandalonePageLayoutPage.tsx:19`.\n- **Adjacent but not the document editor:** the separate TipTap `advanced-text-editor` has typography controls (`getAdvancedTextEditorTypographySettings.ts:4-44`: text color, font size, line height, letter spacing, alignment) and columns (`AdvancedTextEditorBlockCatalog.ts:51-104`). It is used for form/AI/email editing (e.g. `FormRichTextFieldInput.tsx:1,39-49`), **not** the BlockNote record/document editor.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Text review / tracked changes / accept-reject suggestions\n\n**Tracked changes / suggestion mode / accept-reject of individual edits: absent.**\n- No BlockNote suggestion package is installed (`@blocknote/xl-suggestion` not present/listed); the only lockfile `suggestion` match is `@tiptap/suggestion` for menus (`yarn.lock:19993-19995`) and `prosemirror-changeset` as a TipTap transitive (`yarn.lock:19951,43632`).\n- No suggestion/track-changes logic in `blocknote-editor` or the a2e-documents source.\n\nWhat does exist (distinct features):\n- **Version history**: read-only block-level diff + whole-version `Restore` — `BlockEditorVersionHistoryPanel.tsx:119-124` (`getBlockLevelDiff`), `:138-163` (restore entire version), `:193-212` (renders added/changed/removed); diff model at `getBlockLevelDiff.ts:13-19,54-107`. This is not per-change accept/reject.\n- **Comments**: BlockNote `CommentsExtension` with persisted threads — `RichTextFieldEditor.tsx:18,185-192,203`; `blocknote-editor/comments/*`.\n- **Co-editing save conflict** offers whole-document keep-local vs use-remote, not per-edit review — `RichTextFieldEditor.tsx:309-345,442-450`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Embed / record-reference block\n\n**No embed or record-reference *block* exists.**\n- `BLOCK_SCHEMA` block specs are only `defaultBlockSpecs + callout + file` (`Schema.ts:12-16`); `defaultBlockSpecs` contains no `embed`/`recordReference` (`defaultBlocks.d.ts:2-191`). The dashboard schema likewise has none (`DashboardBlockSchema.ts:3-13`).\n- Record references exist solely as the inline `mention` spec (`MentionInlineContent.tsx:84-139`), which renders a chip, not a record view: `MentionRecordChip` (`:118-127`) or legacy `RecordChip` (`:73-80`).\n- The `/link-to-record` slash item inserts that inline mention, not a block: `LinkToRecordPicker.tsx:51-85` (`editor.insertInlineContent([{ type: 'mention', ... }])` at `:72-84`); item definition `LinkToRecordSlashMenuItem.tsx:34-44`.\n- `FileBlock` embeds uploaded files/attachments, not records: `FileBlock.tsx:41-124`.\n- In a2e-documents, record views live **outside** the editor as page-layout widgets/front components: `document.page-layout.ts:23-46` (`FIELDS`, `FIELD_RICH_TEXT`, and a `FRONT_COMPONENT` \"Page\"), `document-page.front-component.tsx:218-338`. There is no editor block that renders a native Twenty record view.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of explicitly absent capabilities\n- Multi-column blocks in the app editor (package installed transitively, not wired) — **absent**.\n- Math/KaTeX/LaTeX rendering — **absent**; mermaid/diagram rendering — **absent**.\n- ODT export — **absent**; menu PDF is browser print only (a separate library PDF path exists for notes).\n- Editor font-family/size, page size, margins, headers/footers — **absent**; `a2e-print-editor` has no CSS rule.\n- Tracked changes / suggestion mode / accept-reject individual edits — **absent**.\n- Embed / native record-view block — **absent** (only inline mention chips).\n</task_result>\n</task>"
