harting dependency** — its deps are `@base-ui/react`, `@monaco-editor/react`, `@radix-ui/colors`, `@sniptt/guards`, `@tabler/icons-react`, `clsx`, `react-responsive`, `react-router-dom`, `type-fest`, `zod` (`packages/twenty-ui/package.json:73-84`).\n\n### ProseMirror / Tiptap (transitive, via BlockNote)\n| Package | Version | License |\n|---|---|---|\n| `@tiptap/core`, `@tiptap/pm`, `@tiptap/react` | 3.30.2 | **MIT** |\n| `prosemirror-model` | 1.25.11 | MIT |\n| `prosemirror-state` | 1.4.4 | MIT |\n| `prosemirror-view` | 1.42.2 | MIT |\n| `prosemirror-transform` | 1.12.0 | MIT |\n| `prosemirror-tables` | 1.8.5 | MIT |\n\nEvidence: each `.../node_modules/<pkg>/package.json`. (`prosemirror-highlight` is declared by `@blocknote/core` but is not resolvable at `node_modules/prosemirror-highlight`; likely nested. Not material to the license question.)\n\nAlso relevant to the Mantine renderer: `@mantine/core` 8.3.15 MIT, `@mantine/hooks` 8.3.18 MIT.\n\n## 3. Direct answers\n\n- **Is BlockNote MIT or AGPL?** Neither. Installed core/react/mantine are **MPL-2.0** (`README.md:91`: \"majority ... licensed under the MPL-2.0 ... allows commercial (and closed-source) applications\"; source-file changes must be published). No MIT and no AGPL in the installed BlockNote tree.\n- **Do the `xl-*` exporters differ?** **Yes, decisively.** They are **not MPL-2.0**. Each `xl-*` package declares `\"license\": \"GPL-3.0 OR PROPRIETARY\"`, ships a **GPLv3** LICENSE file, and the README states: \"The XL packages ... are licensed under the GPL-3.0. If you cannot comply with this license and want to use the XL libraries, you'll need a commercial license\" (`node_modules/@blocknote/core/README.md:93`; also `react/README.md:93`). The bundled LICENSE file itself only contains GPLv3 text — the proprietary/commercial option is documented in `package.json` + README, not in the shipped LICENSE.\n- **Repo usage of the GPL xl packages is real, not just declared.** `twenty-front` directly imports them:\n  - `@blocknote/xl-docx-exporter` in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/blocknote-editor/export/utils/exportBlocksToDocxBlob.ts`\n  - `@blocknote/xl-pdf-exporter` in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/command-menu-item/record/single-record/utils/exportBlockNoteEditorToPdf.ts`\n  - Declared at `packages/twenty-front/package.json:35-36`.\n- `@blocknote/xl-math` and `mermaid` are **not installed**, so no license can be verified for them from this tree.\n\n## 4. License policy files\n\n- **No dedicated policy file exists.** No `LICENSE-POLICY`, `LICENSING`, `THIRD_PARTY`, `THIRD-PARTY`, or `NOTICE` file was found anywhere in the repo (glob returned nothing).\n- The only license-related governance is the root `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/LICENSE` (AGPLv3 + inline \"Twenty.com Commercial License\", lines 2-7 and 727-762), plus per-package `LICENSE` files.\n- `yarn.config.cjs` contains no license constraint rules.\n- The task itself is already tracked in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/tasks/prd.json:423` (\"P3.4: native-primitive/license feasibility check for advanced authoring blocks (report-only)\") and `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/PLAN.md:1391`.\n\n## 5. Copyleft / commercial / unclear flags\n\n| Flag | Package(s) | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| ⚠️ **Strong copyleft (GPL-3.0)** | `@blocknote/xl-docx-exporter`, `@blocknote/xl-pdf-exporter`, `@blocknote/xl-multi-column` | Directly imported by `twenty-front` (AGPL-3.0 project). The \"OR PROPRIETARY\" alternative requires a paid commercial license from BlockNote. Bundled LICENSE file is GPLv3 only. This is the material licensing risk of the advanced-editor stack. |\n| ⚠️ **Commercial option** | same three `xl-*` packages | Dual-license: GPL-3.0 **or** proprietary/commercial; README points to `https://www.blocknotejs.org/pricing`. |\n| ⚠️ **Weak/file-level copyleft** | `@blocknote/core`, `@blocknote/react`, `@blocknote/mantine`, `@blocknote/server-util` | MPL-2.0 — allows commercial/closed-source use, but modifications to BlockNote source files must be published. Not viral across the whole app like GPL/AGPL. |\n| ⚠️ **Commercial (first-party)** | Twenty Enterprise files | Root LICENSE: files marked `/* @license Enterprise */` are commercial, not AGPL. |\n| Unclear/custom | none found beyond the `OR PROPRIETARY` string | `OR PROPRIETARY` is not an SPDX identifier; the actual proprietary terms are not shipped in `node_modules` (they live behind BlockNote's pricing page). Evidence does not contain those terms. |\n| Permissive (no flag) | katex, docx, image-meta, @react-pdf/renderer, @nivo/*, @xyflow/react, @tiptap/*, all ProseMirror packages, yjs, y-prosemirror, @mantine/* | MIT/ISC. `d3-shape` is ISC. |\n\nOne caveat on evidence: the `@react-pdf/renderer` package ships no `LICENSE` file, so its `MIT` is established solely from its `package.json` `license` field.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
